#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112cd61c-d6ec-5b21-a43e-abee24d650f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302569} {:answer/id #uuid "12334453-77d2-5dd2-99d3-4f6f14bdfae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302580} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7e4243-0a26-5991-9f01-96b7ce162b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303429} {:answer/id #uuid "c40013df-d378-5245-93a2-10d8db23f392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c7e4243-0a26-5991-9f01-96b7ce162b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303429} :answer-field/id #uuid "13afdc2d-6b3b-5524-8261-72ad27b914fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45f36c65-eecf-50e8-8dca-3548b95a781e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302899} {:answer/id #uuid "67264ce4-9890-51a9-9cc8-0bd8628bdbd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303081} {:answer/id #uuid "8682a994-8464-5273-a469-d10cd58209c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303295} {:answer/id #uuid "89cf5667-29c6-517a-be74-ef409b12293c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8682a994-8464-5273-a469-d10cd58209c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303295} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ad3cfbc-b21d-58d3-bad3-220676ab157d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28361b8e-e41a-5147-9650-48cd1c63fe66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302716} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8d0101-c035-5b9a-8f40-3244438c6f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303508} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fe574b-0131-545e-9eb4-d166f8e72cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303782} {:answer/id #uuid "efb20cea-cfc2-5903-af87-5bbc8f3a74a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5fe574b-0131-545e-9eb4-d166f8e72cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303782} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4012936-5a67-5c5b-9007-eb2b1e0f5daa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ad3fcdc-246d-580f-b053-3062ecfa179a" :question/math-academy-id "q-330877" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eabf843f-76af-5374-87f3-015cd7c21177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eabf843f-76af-5374-87f3-015cd7c21177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365600} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b0824a7-3977-53c2-8ae9-fab24fac62a7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7d357d-8554-535e-9625-2f454e5a740e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365602} {:answer/id #uuid "2014d6d7-4139-5c85-9128-fa0bef9f20e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4e^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2014d6d7-4139-5c85-9128-fa0bef9f20e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4e^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482873} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2490d5f-d96a-5160-b6f7-a7d11c4a92d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a01f2ab9-e122-54f4-be8c-8d60cf41b11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-330893" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}},\\,Φ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & -3{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-10{e}^{-2t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & -3{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}\\cdot 2{e}^{4t}-(-3{e}^{4t})\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{4t} & 3{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-6t}}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{4t} & 3{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{-2t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{-2t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int -10{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -4{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & -3{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question