:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b65edd94-707e-57da-8e41-b0a5aa3ea589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552106} :answer-field/id #uuid "960a3d7d-d66c-5fbe-96fa-5f23ee214e3a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "152935c5-b544-5453-8a8e-4b219d9f4383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551709} {:answer/id #uuid "6640095a-fe8d-5515-9471-248e11fa3c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551904} {:answer/id #uuid "98bc28b4-09b7-5893-b26d-220e451804c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552036} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f07c4f-a021-59c5-b2cb-6c8598378a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "152935c5-b544-5453-8a8e-4b219d9f4383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551709} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcdee848-1598-5289-b462-0d40568a03c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77948b35-77f3-58cd-80e2-2c25a0aff174" :question/math-academy-id "q-336705" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-3}} into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007369ab-f779-5cec-ab3a-4cd8748045f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308746} {:answer/id #uuid "3252b4dc-3d9b-59ec-b811-1e095931c3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309129} {:answer/id #uuid "5b61eaf4-466a-5dc6-ae53-347f04ee8ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309433} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dc9876-d624-583a-b858-f1ff642bd28b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "007369ab-f779-5cec-ab3a-4cd8748045f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308746} :answer-field/id #uuid "86c4d704-7126-5478-933f-e7c2ee88810e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6338b11f-8b1b-5a9e-866f-819a08284c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :ans